  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 430.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": "This is a new independent review of fixed handoff-v004, not reuse of rejected v002 QA. Actually inspected all7 selected source originals on light/dark native composites (two 2-up pairs and five singles), all9 selected poses plus exact adopted neutral on5 inherited430px comparison pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows. Tawny spotted large head/short upright torso, paired tufted pointed ears, pink ear interiors, cheek ruff, white eye surround and brown pupil, cream muzzle/chest/belly, paired rounded forepaws/feet and one short dark-tipped tail are consistent. Fresh blink has close usual head/ear/torso/foot layout, without the earlier sheet blur or visibly elongated torso; happy closed eyelid arches are intentional. Fresh greet raises the connected forepaw; paired left/right presentations extend the appropriate paw with corresponding gaze. Tilted think touches chin with its connected rounded paw; aha holds a compact bent paw without a human pointing finger. Cheer raises both rounded paws, while species phases bring the same paw near the cheek/ear. Pair4 cheer/species_a has small ear-angle/head-width drawing variation (producer notes about5%); at430px this reads as an active expression/gesture and was not judged an obvious identity or anatomical break. There is no claim of pixel-identical head contour across active gestures. All selected facial lines, spots, toe divisions and ear tufts are clear at430px. No clipping, duplicated parts, detached limbs, broad tinted alpha field or dirty paint was seen. Intentional bounded paper texture is preserved. Discrete recipe returns retain the exact usual neutral and show no obvious double limb.",
  "cautions": [
    "Pair4 cheer/species_a retains a small roughly5% ear/head-width variation, accepted here for active poses. Production timing/interpolation must still be assessed in the final animation.",
    "Whole native selected originals and static max-scale/discrete recipe views were observed; real-time playback, final MP4 and physical UI zoom/density were not measured.",
    "Rejected earlier core-sheet and v002 QA remain historical and are not accepted by this review."
  ],
